Oh, that one ranks as a YANI needing more detail:

Topiary Golem: a leafy green ferocious monster unfortunately rooted
to one spot, and thus most dangerous when the adventurer walks straight
into it. Never occurs in corridors (due to the poor lighting).

Typically found in open areas such as the big room, mine town central,
mines bottom central, upper quest levels, the castle level,
Fort Ludious, the swampy Medusa level, and the like.

Usual subspecies are giant-dog-o-form, giraffe-o-form, ox-o-form,
1939-Ford-coupe-o-form, squirrel-o-form, dolphin-form, and the like.

The most dangerous of all, of course, is the Imvisible Topiary Golem,
or giant-Harvey-the-Rabbit-o-form.

Color blind adventurers, 10% of all males, are especially prone to
mistaking Topiary Golems for snacks-on-the-hoof.

Vegan pets and Topiary Golems should be kept apart if at all
possible; Bad Things Will Happen otherwise, more often to the
pet, nearly irresistably attracted to topiary golems.

Likely to provide small vegan-diet treasures to adventurers wielding
pruning hooks, which do negative damage to topiary golems. [This
should only be attempted by a)pplying the pruning hook from a safe
distance, and with adequate dexterity.]

Frequently found in the company of peaceful wood nymphs (dryads),
who turn hostile in a heartbeat if the topiary golem is attacked
or mis-trimmed or browsed by your pet.

See also: Wait-a-Bit Bush, Edward Scissorshands, Tangle Tree.

